    "result_text": "The only executable test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are a base class and a helper). The full suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the telephone-uniqueness rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:104`).\n\nThe endpoint already normalized the incoming telephone by stripping non-digits and requiring exactly 10 digits. I added a check right after that: it iterates existing owners, normalizes each stored telephone the same way, and returns **409 Conflict** if any other owner already uses that normalized number. Only if none matches does it proceed to save.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass:\n- `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` \u2014 duplicate telephone \u2192 409.\n- `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` \u2014 distinct telephones \u2192 2xx.\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
